ascending start, then ascending call_id\\n    sorted_calls = sorted(calls, key=lambda x: (-x['score'], x['start'], x['call_id']))\\n    \\n    selected = []\\n    selected_spans = []  # list of (start, end) tuples\\n    \\n    for c in sorted_calls:\\n        start = c['start']\\n        end = c['end']\\n        # Check overlap with any already selected\\n        overlap = False\\n        for s_start, s_end in selected_spans:\\n            if not (end <= s_start or start >= s_end):\\n                overlap = True\\n                break\\n        if not overlap:\\n            selected.append(c)\\n            selected_spans.append((start, end))\\n    \\n    # Order selected calls by start for output\\n    selected_sorted_by_start = sorted(selected, key=lambda x: (x['start'], x['call_id']))\\n    selected_call_ids = [c['call_id'] for c in selected_sorted_by_start]\\n    \\n    # Apply replacements from right to left (by start descending)\\n    result_tokens = list(tokens)\\n    for c in sorted(selected, key=lambda x: -x['start']):\\n        start = c['start']\\n        end = c['end']\\n        repl = c['replacement_tokens']\\n        result_tokens[start:end] = repl\\n    \\n    return {\\n        \\\"selected_call_ids\\\": selected_call_ids,\\n        \\\"tokens\\\": result_tokens\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that takes a payload object with fields: tokens (list of strings), calls (list of dicts with call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens). The objective: select non-overlapping calls based on descending score, then start, then call_id. Then apply replacements from right to left to produce interleaved tokens. Return selected_call_ids (list of string call_ids in order of start position) and tokens (list of strings after replacements). Must follow output schema exactly. No extra fields.\n\nImplementation details:\n- Input case has keys: tokens, calls. Possibly _case_nonce but ignore.\n- Validate: tokens list of strings, 